hadiths[114]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2610","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) would remain in prostration for as long as it takes a person to recite fifty verses. The narrator states: Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) meant that he used to do this in the voluntary night prayer."
"2611","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to observe thirteen rak'ahs of the night prayer. Five out of them consisted of Witr, and he did not sit, but at the end (for salutation). (Using translation from Muslim 737a)"
"2612","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) used to perform eleven rak'ahs from after the 'Isha prayer, which people call 'Atamah, until Fajr. He would say salam after every two rak'ahs. He would perform Witr with a single rak'ah. When the muezzin would finish giving the adhan for Fajr and the true dawn had appeared and the muezzin would come, he (the Prophet) would get up and perform two short rak'ahs, then he would lie down on his right side until the muezzin would come to call him."
"2613","The Prophet (peace be upon him) would not pray more than eleven rak'ahs in Ramadan or outside of Ramadan."
"2614","Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray eleven rakʿat at night and that was his night prayer and each of his prostrations lasted for a period enough for one of you to recite fifty verses before Messenger of Allah ﷺ raised his head. He also used to pray two rakʿat (Sunnah) before the (compulsory) Fajr prayer and then lie down on his right side till the Mu'adh-dhin came to him for the prayer. (Using translation from Bukhārī 994)"
"2615","“The Prophet ﷺ used to pray thirteen Rak’ah at night.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1359)"
"2616","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) used to offer eight (nafl) rak'ahs at night and one rak'ah of witr, then he would sit and offer two rak'ahs."
"2617","narrates: If we wished to see the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) performing voluntary prayers at night, we would see him performing them, and if we wished to see him sleeping at night, we would see him sleeping as well."
"2618","Anas bin Malik was asked about the Prophet's fasting and he said: ""He would fast during a month until we thought that he did not want to abstain from fasting during any of it. And, he would not fast during a month until we thought that he did not want to fast during any of it. (There was no time) that I wanted to see if he was performing Salat during the night, except that I would see him praying, nor to see him sleeping, except that I would see him sleeping."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 769)"
"2619","Al-Aswad ibn Yazid said that he entered upon Aisha and asked her about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the night. She said: He used to pray thirteen rak'ahs during the night. Then he began to pray eleven rak'ahs and left two rak'ahs. When he died, he would pray nine rak'ahs during the night. His last prayer during the night was witr. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1363)"
"2620","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) was asked, ""What do you command us regarding how we should perform prayer at night?"" The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You should perform the prayer two by two. When you fear that dawn is near, then perform one rak'ah as witr."
"2621","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) used to perform one rak'ah of Witr."
"2622","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: Perform the night prayer in sets of two rak‘ahs, and when you fear that dawn is near, then perform one rak‘ah; in this way, you will make your night prayer odd-numbered."
"2623","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) replied: It should be performed two by two, and when you fear that dawn is near, then perform one rak'ah and two prostrations before the break of dawn."
"2624","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Prayer at night is two by two, then when you want to finish, pray one rak'h which will make the total number that you prayed odd."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1692)"
"2625","The Prophet ﷺ said: ""Witr is one rak'ah at the end of the night."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1689)"
"2626","I slept (one night) in the house of Maimuna, the wife of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was with her that night. He (after sleeping for half of the night got up and) then performed ablution and then stood up and observed prayer. I too stood on his left side. He took hold of me and made me stand on his right side. He (the Holy Prophet) observed thirteen rakʿahs on that night. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then slept and snored and it was a habit with him to snore while sleeping. The Mu'adhdhin then came to him (to inform him about the prayer). He then went out and observed prayer without performing ablution. (ʿAmr said: Bukair b. Ashajj had narrated it to me ) (Using translation from Muslim 763d)"
"2627","I got up, performed ablution, and came to stand on his left side. The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) pulled me and made me stand on his right side. The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) performed thirteen rak‘ahs, in which his standing was equal."
"2628","I took hold of his mount's reins and made his camel sit down. The Prophet (peace be upon him) stood up and performed the Isha prayer. Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) was at his side. The Prophet (peace be upon him) performed thirteen rak'ahs."
"2629","I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he made his mount sit down, then he dismounted and performed ten rak‘ahs, two at a time. Then he performed one rak‘ah of witr, then he performed two rak‘ahs (sunnah) of Fajr, then he performed the morning (Fajr) prayer."
"2630","I never saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ reciting the Quraan in his prayer at night in sitting condition until he became old. Then he used to sit in it (the prayer) and recite the Quran until forty or thirty verses remained, then he stood and recited them and prostrated himself. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 953)"
"2631","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray standing at night for a long time, and used to pray sitting at night for a long time. When he prayed standing, he bowed standing, and when he prayed sitting, he bowed sitting. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 955)"
"2632","“I did not see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ offer any of the night prayers in any way other than standing, until he became old. Then he started to pray sitting down until, when there were thirty or forty Verses left of his recitation, he would stand up and recite them, and prostrate.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1227)"
"2633","""I never saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray sitting down until he grew old. Then he would pray sitting down and when there were thirty or forty verses left, he would stand up and recite them, then bow."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1649)"
"2634","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) used to perform eight rak‘ahs, then he would perform witr, then he would sit and perform two rak‘ahs, then he would stand and recite (Qur’an), then go into ruku‘, then between the adhan and iqamah of the morning prayer he would perform two rak‘ahs (sunnah)."
"2635","The water for his ablution and his miswak would be placed near his head. Then he would wake up, use the miswak, perform ablution, and offer prayer, two short rak’ahs. Then he would stand and offer eight rak’ahs in which he would recite an equal amount in each. Then he would make them odd by performing witr with the ninth rak’ah. Then he would sit and offer two rak’ahs. When the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) became older and his body became heavier, he reduced the eight rak’ahs to six and would perform witr with the seventh rak’ah. Then he would sit and offer two rak’ahs in which he would recite Surah Al-Kafiroon and Surah Az-Zalzalah."
"2636","One night I slept at the house of Maimuna. The Prophet ﷺ woke up, answered the call of nature, washed his face and hands, and then slept. He got up (late at night), went to a water skin, opened the mouth thereof and performed ablution not using much water, yet he washed all the parts properly and then offered the prayer. I got up and straightened my back in order that the Prophet ﷺ might not feel that I was watching him, and then I performed the ablution, and when he got up to offer the prayer, I stood on his left. He caught hold of my ear and brought me over to his right side. He offered thirteen rakʿat in all and then lay down and slept till he started blowing out his breath as he used to do when he slept. In the meantime Bilal informed the Prophet ﷺ of the approaching time for the (Fajr) prayer, and the Prophet offered the Fajr (Morning) prayer without performing new ablution. He used to say in his invocation, Allahumma ijʿal fi qalbi nuran wa fi basari nuran, wa fi samʿi nuran, waʿan yamini nuran, waʿan yasari nuran, wa fawqi nuran, wa tahti nuran, wa amami nuran, wa khalfi nuran, wajʿal li nuran."" Kuraib (a sub narrator) said, ""I have forgotten seven other words, (which the Prophet ﷺ mentioned in this invocation). I met a man from the offspring of Al-ʿAbbas and he narrated those seven things to me, mentioning, '(Let there be light in) my nerves, my flesh, my blood, my hair and my body,' and he also mentioned two other things."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 6316)"
"2637","When he was with me he would sleep at dawn. By this she referred to the Prophet ﷺ. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1318)"
"2638","""I asked 'Aishah about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. She said: 'He used to sleep during the first part of the night, then get up during the time before dawn and pray witr. Then he would go to his bed and if he needed to be intimate he would go to his wife. Then when he heard the Adhan he would get up, and if he was junub he would pour water over himself, otherwise he would perform wudu, then he would go out to the prayer.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1680)"
"2639","""He used to pray 'Isha, then he would recite tasbih, then after that he would pray whatever Allah (SWT) willed (he should pray) of night prayer. Then he would go and sleep for as long as he had prayed. Then he would get up from sleep and pray for as long as he had slept, and this last prayer of his would continue until dawn."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1628)"
"2640","The water for his ablution and his miswak would be placed near his head. Then he would wake up and use the miswak, then perform ablution and offer prayer. He would first offer two short rak’ahs, then he would offer eight rak’ahs in which he would recite almost equal portions (of the Qur’an). He would make them odd by performing a ninth rak’ah. Then he would sit and offer two rak’ahs. When the Prophet (peace be upon him) grew older and his body became heavier, he started offering six rak’ahs instead of eight, and would make them odd by performing a seventh rak’ah. Then he would sit and offer two rak’ahs in which he would recite Surah Al-Kafiroon and Surah Az-Zalzalah."
"2641","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Abdullah bin Amr! Do not be like that person who used to offer voluntary prayers at night but then abandoned the night prayer."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) In this narration, there is evidence that it is permissible for a person to say something about another person in his absence, which, if that person were to hear it, would make him sad, as long as the intention of the speaker is not to disparage him but rather to warn someone else in some regard."
"2642","Lady Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Whenever the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) performed any deed, he would do it regularly. If he slept at night or could not perform the night prayers due to illness, he would perform twelve rak'ahs during the day. Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: I never saw the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) performing voluntary prayers for the entire night until dawn, nor did I ever see him fasting continuously for a whole month except in the month of Ramadan. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) This narration contains evidence that Witr is not obligatory, because if it were obligatory, he would have performed the thirteen rak'ahs of the night during the day."
"2643","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ as saying: He who misses him daily round of recital or part of it due to sleep and he recites it between the dawn and the noon prayers, will be reckoned as if he recited it at night. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1313)"
"2644","I never saw the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) performing voluntary prayers for the entire night until dawn, nor did I see him fasting for a whole month except in the month of Ramadan."
"2645","When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not pray at night because he was prevented from doing so by sleep- meaning, sleep overwhelmed him- or by pain, he would pray twelve rak'ahs during the day. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1789)"
"2646","'A'isha reported that when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ decided upon doing any act, he continued to do it, and when he slept at night or fell sick he observed twelve rak'ahs during the daytime. I am not aware of Messenger of Allah ﷺ observing prayer during the whole of the night till morning, or observing fast for a whole month continuously except that of Ramadan. (Using translation from Muslim 746f)"
"2647","""The Messenger of Allah said: 'Whoever forgets a prayer, let him perform it when he remembers it.'"" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 696)"
"2648","The Prophet ﷺ said, ""If anyone forgets a prayer he should pray that prayer when he remembers it. There is no expiation except to pray the same."" Then he recited: ""Establish prayer for My (i.e. Allah's) remembrance."" (20.14). (Using translation from Bukhārī 597)"
"2649","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) and his companions slept through the night, so the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: You all should perform it tomorrow at its (prescribed) time."
"2650","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Mount your rides. Then he mounted, and we also mounted. He traveled for a while, and when the sun had risen high, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dismounted. He ordered Sayyiduna Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him), and he gave the call to prayer (adhan). The people fulfilled their needs and performed ablution. They offered two units (rak‘ahs) of (Sunnah) prayer. Then Sayyiduna Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him) gave the iqamah. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in prayer. We said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), should we not make up this prayer at its time tomorrow? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your Lord has forbidden you from usury, so would He Himself accept it?"
"2651","""We stopped to camp at the end of the night with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and we did not wake up until the sun had risen. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Let each man take hold of his camel's head (and leave), for the Shaitan was here in this place with us.' We did that, then he called for water and performed Wudu', then he prayed two Rak'ahs, then the Iqamah was said and he prayed Al-Ghadah (Fajr)."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 623)"
"2652","It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that the Prophet ﷺ slept and missed the two Rak’ah before Fajr, so he made them up after the sun had risen. (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1155)"
"2653","I asked: Today you performed such a prayer which you have not performed before. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) replied: Some wealth had come to me, so due to being occupied, I was not able to perform these two rak‘ahs before ‘Asr as I used to do previously, so I have performed them now. I asked: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), if these rak‘ahs are missed by us, should we make them up? The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: No."
"2654","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) concluded the ‘Asr prayer after performing three rak‘ahs. Sayyiduna Khirbaq said to him: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! Did you forget, or has the prayer been shortened? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Did Khirbaq speak the truth? The people replied: Yes! So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) stood up and performed one rak‘ah, then he performed two prostrations of forgetfulness, and then he concluded with salam."
"2655","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) called the two prostrations of forgetfulness two things that disgrace (the devil)."
"2656","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) led us in prayer. He either added something to it or perhaps omitted something. When th"
"2657","""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed and did more or less (rak'ahs). When he had said the taslim, it was said: 'O Messenger of Allah, has there been some change concerning the prayer?' He said: 'If there had been some change concerning the prayer, I would have told you. Rather I am a human being and I forget as you forget. If any one of you is not sure about his prayer, let him consider an estimate of what is correct, and complete his prayer on that basis, then say the taslim and prostrate twice.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1242)"
"2658","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) inquired: What has happened? They said: You have led five rak'ahs. So the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) performed two prostrations of forgetfulness after concluding the prayer with salam."
"2659","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""When a person has doubt regarding his prayer, he should try to estimate the correct situation, then say the salam, and then perform two prostrations of forgetfulness (sajda sahw)."
"2660","""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed and did more or less (rak'ahs). When he had said the taslim, it was said: 'O Messenger of Allah, has there been some change concerning the prayer?' He said: 'If there had been some change concerning the prayer, I would have told you. Rather I am a human being and I forget as you forget. If any one of you is not sure about his prayer, let him consider an estimate of what is correct, and complete his prayer on that basis, then say the taslim and prostrate twice.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1242)"
"2661","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"2662","The Prophet ﷺ prayed (and the sub-narrator Ibrahim said, ""I do not know whether he prayed more or less than usual""), and when he had finished the prayers he was asked, ""O Messenger of Allah ﷺ! Has there been any change in the prayers?"" He said, ""What is it?' The people said, ""You have prayed so much and so much."" So the Prophet ﷺ bent his legs, faced the Qibla and performed two prostration's (of Sahu) and finished his prayers with Taslim (by turning his face to right and left saying: 'As-Salamu ʿAlaikum- Warahmat-ullah'). When he turned his face to us he said, ""If there had been anything changed in the prayer, surely I would have informed you but I am a human being like you and liable to forget like you. So if I forget remind me and if anyone of you is doubtful about his prayer, he should follow what he thinks to be correct and complete his prayer accordingly and finish it and do two prostrations (of Sahu). (Using translation from Bukhārī 401)"
"2663","The Prophet ﷺ said: When one of you is in doubt about his prayer, and does not know how much he has prayed, three or four rak'ahs, he should pray one (additional) rak'ah and make two prostrations while sitting before giving the salutation. If the (additional) rak'ah which he prayed is the fifth one, he will make it an even number by these two prostrations. If it is the fourth one, the two prostrations will be a disgrace for the devil. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1026)"
"2664","“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘If anyone of you is uncertain about his prayer, let him put aside uncertainty and act upon that which is certain. When he has made sure his prayer is complete, then let him prostrate twice. Then if his prayer was complete, that (extra) Rak’ah will be counted as voluntary, and if his prayer was lacking, that Rak’ah will complete his prayer, and the two prostrations will rub the Satan’s nose in the dust.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1210)"
"2665","narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When a person offers prayer and is unsure whether he has performed three rak'ahs or four, then while he is sitting, he should perform two prostrations of forgetfulness, because Satan comes to a person and says, 'You have become impure (lost your wudu),' so that person should say, 'You are lying.' However, if he hears a sound (of passing wind) with his ears or perceives a smell with his nose, (then the ruling is different)."
"2666","narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When Satan comes to any one of you and says, 'You have lost your wudu,' then he should say in his mind, 'You are lying,' until a person hears the sound (of passing wind) with his ear or perceives its smell with his nose (he should not perform wudu again until then)."
"2667","“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘If anyone of you is uncertain about his prayer, let him put aside uncertainty and act upon that which is certain. When he has made sure his prayer is complete, then let him prostrate twice. Then if his prayer was complete, that (extra) Rak’ah will be counted as voluntary, and if his prayer was lacking, that Rak’ah will complete his prayer, and the two prostrations will rub the Satan’s nose in the dust.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1210)"
"2668","The Prophet ﷺ said: When one of you is in doubt about his prayer, and does not know how much he has prayed, three or four rak'ahs, he should pray one (additional) rak'ah and make two prostrations while sitting before giving the salutation. If the (additional) rak'ah which he prayed is the fifth one, he will make it an even number by these two prostrations. If it is the fourth one, the two prostrations will be a disgrace for the devil. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1026)"
"2669","The narration transmitted from Sayyiduna Abdullah ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) and Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) is the narration that caused a learned person to fall into the misunderstanding that making an estimation (taharrī) during prayer and acting upon certainty (yaqīn) are the same thing. Whereas the rulings of both are different. In the narration transmitted from Sayyiduna Abdullah ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him), there is the ruling of estimation (taharrī), in which the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered to perform two prostrations of forgetfulness after the salām. Whereas in the narration transmitted from Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him), there is the ruling of acting upon certainty (yaqīn), in which the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered to perform the prostrations of forgetfulness before the salām. So, there is a difference between making an estimation (taharrī) and acting upon certainty (yaqīn). Because acting upon certainty means that if a person is in doubt about his prayer and does not know whether he has performed three rak'ahs or four, when such a situation arises, he will act upon what he is certain of, and that is three rak'ahs. Then he will complete his prayer and perform two prostrations of forgetfulness before the salām. As for estimation (taharrī), its situation is that a person starts the prayer, then his mind becomes occupied with some worldly or religious matter to the extent that he does not know how much of the prayer he has performed. When such a situation arises, he will make an estimation according to what is most likely, and whatever is established for him as a result of this estimation, he will act upon it, then complete his prayer and perform two prostrations of forgetfulness after the salām. In this way, both narrations can be acted upon together."
"2670","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led those people in prayer. He performed the prostration of forgetfulness (sajda sahw)"
"2671","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) concluded the ‘Asr prayer after three rak‘ahs. Sayyiduna Khirbaq (may Allah be pleased"
"2672","The Prophet ﷺ led them in prayer and forgot something, so he made prostrations and uttered the tashahhud, then gave the salutation. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1039)"
"2673","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) led three rak‘ahs in either Zuhr or ‘Asr prayer (and concluded with salam). This was brought to his attention, so he asked: “Is it so?” The people replied: “Yes.” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) then performed one rak‘ah, recited tashahhud, and concluded with salam. Then he performed two prostrations of forgetfulness (sajda sahw), and then concluded with salam."
"2674","The Prophet (peace be upon him) made a mistake and ended the prayer with salam after two rak‘ahs. When the Prophet (peace be upon him) completed the prayer, a man said to him: O Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)! You made a mistake; you ended the prayer with salam after two rak‘ahs. So the Prophet (peace be upon him) ordered Sayyiduna Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him), who then gave the iqamah for prayer, and the Prophet (peace be upon him) completed that one rak‘ah. I asked the people about the person who had said: O Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), you made a mistake. I was asked: Do you know him? I replied: No. If I see him, I will recognize him. Then a man passed by me and I said: This is the man. It was said: This is Sayyiduna Talhah bin Ubaidullah (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"2675","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in one of the evening (‘Asha) prayers, noon or afternoon. He led us in two Rak’ahs and gave the salutation. He then got up going towards a piece of wood which was placed in the front part of the mosque. He placed his hands upon it, one on the other, looking from his face as if he were angry. The people came out hastily saying: the prayer has been shortened. Abu Bakr and ‘Umar were among the people, but they were too afraid to speak to him. A man whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would call “ the possessor of arms” (Dhu al-Yadain) stood up (asking him): Have you forgotten. The Messenger of Allah, or has the prayer been shortened? He said: I have neither forgotten nor has it been shortened. He said : Messenger of Allah , you have forgotten. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned towards the people and asked : did the possessor of arms speak the truth? They made a sign , that is, yes. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned to his place and prayed the remaining two Rak’ahs, then gave the salutation; he then uttered the takbir and prostrated himself as usual or prolonged. He then raised his head and uttered the takbir; then he uttered the takbir and made prostration as usual or made longer (prostration). Then he raised his head his and uttered the takbir (Allah is most great). The narrator Muhammad was asked : Did he give the salutation (while prostrating) dueto forgetfulness? He said : I do not remember it from Abu Hurairah. But we Are sure that ‘Imran b. Husain (in his version) said; he then gave the salutation. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1008)"
"2676","Once Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in the Zuhr prayer and got up (after the prostrations of the second rakʿa) although he should have sat (for the Tashahhud). So at the end of the prayer, he prostrated twice while sitting (prostrations of Sahu). (Using translation from Bukhārī 830)"
"2677","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) stood up after performing two rak‘ahs instead of sitting. The people also stood up with him. When he sat after performing four rak‘ahs and the people were waiting for him to say salam, he said takbeer, then went into prostration, then said takbeer, then went into prostration again. This happened before he said salam."
"2678","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up in the noon prayer (though) he hadith sit (after the two rak'ahs). When he completed the prayer he performed two prostrations and said,"" Allah is the Most Great"" in each prostration, while he was sitting before pronouncing salutation, and the people performed prostration along with him. That was a compensation for he had forgotten to observe jalsa (after two rak'ahs). (Using translation from Muslim 570b)"
"2679","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) stood up after performing two rak‘ahs of the Zuhr prayer. He did not sit down. When he completed the prayer, he performed two prostrations of forgetfulness (sajda sahw), and then he gave salam."
"2680","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) performed prayer. After completing two rak‘ahs, he stood up. When he was supposed to sit, we said ""Subhan Allah,"" but he continued the prayer. When he finished the prayer and was sitting, he performed two prostrations of forgetfulness (sajda sahw)."
"2681","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) led them in five rak'ahs. When he finished with salam, this was mentioned to him. So he turned towards the qiblah, and while sitting, he performed the prostration of forgetfulness (sajdah sahw) twice."
"2682","The people said: You have led five rak'ahs. So the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) performed two prostrations of forgetfulness (sajda sahw) after concluding the prayer with salam."
"2683","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) say: \""Satan comes to one of you while he is performing prayer. He comes so that he may make his prayer doubtful for him, to the extent that a person does not know how much he has prayed. When someone faces such a situation, then when he is sitting, he should perform two prostrations of forgetfulness (sajda sahw).\"""""
"2684","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in the Zuhr or Asr prayer, and after performing two rak‘ahs, he said the salam."
"2685","""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed Zuhr or 'Asr and said the taslim following two rak'ahs and left. Dhul-Shimalain bin 'Amr said to him: 'Has the prayer been shortened or did you forget?"" The Prophet ﷺ said: 'What is Dhul-Yadain saying?' They said: 'He is speaking the truth, O Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' So he led them in praying the two rak'ahs that he missed."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1230)"
"2686","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished praying two rak'ahs,and Dhul-Yadain said to him: ""Has the prayer been shortened or did you forget, O Messenger of Allah?"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Is Dhul-Yadain speaking the truth?"" The people said: ""Yes."" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up and prayed two, then he said the takbir and prostrated as usual or longer than that. Then he raised his head, then he prostrated as usual or longer than that, then he sat up."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1225)"
"2687","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Neither of the two has happened. He said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! You led us in only two rak‘ahs. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked: What is Dhul-Yadain saying? He turned to those present and they said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! You led us in only two rak‘ahs. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) stood up, faced the qiblah, and performed the remaining two rak‘ahs, then concluded with salam. Then, while sitting, he performed two prostrations of forgetfulness (sujood as-sahw)."
"2688","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in one of the evening (‘Asha) prayers, noon or afternoon. He led us in two Rak’ahs and gave the salutation. He then got up going towards a piece of wood which was placed in the front part of the mosque. He placed his hands upon it, one on the other, looking from his face as if he were angry. The people came out hastily saying: the prayer has been shortened. Abu Bakr and ‘Umar were among the people, but they were too afraid to speak to him. A man whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would call “ the possessor of arms” (Dhu al-Yadain) stood up (asking him): Have you forgotten. The Messenger of Allah, or has the prayer been shortened? He said: I have neither forgotten nor has it been shortened. He said : Messenger of Allah , you have forgotten. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned towards the people and asked : did the possessor of arms speak the truth? They made a sign , that is, yes. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned to his place and prayed the remaining two Rak’ahs, then gave the salutation; he then uttered the takbir and prostrated himself as usual or prolonged. He then raised his head and uttered the takbir; then he uttered the takbir and made prostration as usual or made longer (prostration). Then he raised his head his and uttered the takbir (Allah is most great). The narrator Muhammad was asked : Did he give the salutation (while prostrating) dueto forgetfulness? He said : I do not remember it from Abu Hurairah. But we Are sure that ‘Imran b. Husain (in his version) said; he then gave the salutation. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1008)"
"2689","The Prophet ﷺ named the two prostrations of forgetfulness disgraceful for the devil. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1025)"
"2690","When the people encamped, (the narrator Amr ibn Uthman al-Himsi) said: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ encamped, the people scattered in the glens and wadis. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Your scattering in these glens and wadis is only of the devil. They afterwards kept close together when they encamped to such an extent that it used to be said that if a cloth were spread over them, it would cover them all. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2628)"
"2691","narrates: Previously, people used to go for Hajj without taking provisions along with them, so Allah Almighty revealed this verse: ""And take provisions with you; indeed, the best provision is piety."
"2692","I advise you to adopt the fear of Allah Almighty and to say ""Allahu Akbar"" (Allah is the Greatest) upon every elevation you ascend. The narrator says: When that man left, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) prayed: O Allah! Fold the earth for him and make his journey easy for him."
"2693","I was about to depart for Iraq, and there was another person with me. Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) came with us to see us off. When he was about to part from us, he said: I have nothing with me to give you, but I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) say this: ""When a person entrusts something to Allah Almighty, Allah protects it. So I entrust your religion, your trust, and the end of your deeds to Allah Almighty."
"2694","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is a devil on the back of every camel. When you ride it, mention the name of Allah and do not be negligent regarding your need."
"2695","When the Prophet ﷺ wanted to travel, when he mounted his riding camel, he would say the Takbir three times and say: Glory is to Him Who has subjected this to us, and we were not able to do it. And, surely, to our Lord are we returning (Subḥān alladhī sakh-khara lanā hādhā wa mā kunnā lahū muqrinīn. Wa innā ilā rabbinā lamunqalibūn). Then he would say: “O Allah, I ask You in this journey of mine from the righteousness and piety and actions that which you are pleased with. O Allah, ease for us the path, and make near for us the distance of the land. O Allah, You are the companion in the journey, and the caretaker for the family. O Allah, accompany us in our journey, and take care of our families (Allāhumma innī as’aluka fī safarī hādhā minal-birri wat-taqwā, wa minal-ʿamali mā tarḍā. Allāhumma hawwin ʿalainal-masīra, waṭwi ʿannā buʿdal-arḍ. Allāhumma antaṣ-ṣāḥibu fis safari wal-khalīfatu fil-ahli. Allāhumma aṣḥabnā fī safarinā wakhlufnā fī ahlinā).” And when he would return to his family, he would say: “(We are) Returning, if Allah wills, repenting, worshipping, and to our Lord directing the praise (Ā’ibūna in shā’ Allāh, tā’ibūna ʿābidūna lirabbinā hāmidūn).” (Using translation from Tirmidhī 3447)"
"2696","Hallowed is He Who subdued for us this (ride) and we were not ourselves powerful enough to use It as a ride, and we are going to return to our Lord. O Allah, we seek virtue and piety from Thee in this journey of ours and the act which pleaseth Thee. O Allah, lighten this journey of ours, and make its distance easy for us. O Allah, Thou art (our) companion during the journey, and guardian of (our) family. O Allah, I seek refuge with Thee from hardships of the journey, gloominess of the sights, and finding of evil changes in property and family on return. And he (the Holy Prophet) uttered (these words), and made this addition to them: We are returning, repentant, worshipping our Lord. and praising Him. (Using translation from Muslim 1342)"
"2697","I was riding behind him."
"2698","I saw ‘Ali ؓ when a mount was brought to him to ride. When he put his foot in the stirrup, he said: Bismillah (in the Name of Allah). When he got on it, he said: Glory be to the One Who has placed this (transport) at our service and we ourselves would not have been capable of that, and to our Lord is our final destiny. Then he said Alhamdulillah three times and Allahu Akbar three times, then he said: Glory be to You, there is no god but You. I have indeed wronged myself, so forgive me. Then he smiled, and I said: Why are you smiting, O Ameer al-Muʿmimeen? He said: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do what I have done, then he smiled and I said: Why are you smiling O Messenger of Allah ﷺ He said: ʿThe Lord marvels at His slave when he says, ʿLord forgive me,ʿ and He says: ʿMy slave knows that no one forgives sins but Me.ʿ (Using translation from Aḥmad 753)"
"2699","""Three supplications are accepted , there is no doubt in them (about them being accepted): The supplication of the oppressed, the supplication of the traveler, and the supplication of a parent against his child."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 1905)"
"2700","“If anyone of you, when he stops to camp (while on a journey), says A’udhu bi kalimatil-lahit-tammati min sharri ma khalaq (I seek refuge in the Perfect Words of Allah from the evil of that which He has created), then nothing will harm him in that place until he moves on.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3547)"
"2701","Let a hearer hear beginning with praise of Allah and His good favours and blessing to us. Our Lord, accompany us and show favour to us, and I seek refuge in Allah from Hell. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 5086)"
"2702","I advise you to adopt the fear of Allah, and to say 'Allahu Akbar' (Allah is the Greatest) when ascending every height."" When that man departed, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) prayed: ""O Allah! Fold the earth for him and make his journey easy for him."
"2703","When you journey through a fertile land, you should (go slow and) give the camels a chance to graze in the land. When you travel In an arid (land) where there is scarcity of vegetation, you should quicken their pace (lest your camels grow feeble and emaciated for lack of fodder). When you halt for the night, avoid (pitching your tent on) the road, for it is the abode of noxious little animals at night. (Using translation from Muslim 1926a)"
"2704","narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""If these people knew (how much harm there is) in traveling alone, then no rider would ever travel alone at night."
"2705","When you journey through a fertile land, you should (go slow and) give the camels a chance to graze in the land. When you travel In an arid (land) where there is scarcity of vegetation, you should quicken their pace (lest your camels grow feeble and emaciated for lack of fodder). When you halt for the night, avoid (pitching your tent on) the road, for it is the abode of noxious little animals at night. (Using translation from Muslim 1926a)"
"2706","The people were fasting, some were walking, and some were riding. It was submitted to the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): Fasting is causing hardship for the people, and they are waiting to see what you will do. So the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked for a bowl, raised it towards his mouth until the people saw it, and then he drank from it. After that, some people broke their fast, while others remained fasting. It was submitted to the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): Some people are still fasting. The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Those people are disobedient. Among the companions of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), those who were walking gathered together. They said: We are seeking the supplications of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), while the journey has become intense and the hardship prolonged. So the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Seek help by walking quickly, for it cuts off the marks of the earth; this will be easier for you. The narrator says: We did so, and it became easier for us."
"2707","‘Abd Allah bin ‘Umar said “When the Apostle of Allaah ﷺ returned from an expedition, Hajj or ‘Umrah on every rising piece of ground he would say three times “Allaah is Most Great” and he would say “There is no god bt Allaah alone who has no partner, to Whom the dominion belongs, to Whom praise is due, and Who is Omnipotent, serving, prostrating ourselves before our Lord and expressing praise. Allaah alone has kept his word, helped His servant and routed the confederate. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2770)"
"2708","Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ""Journey is a piece of torture, for it disturbs one's sleep, eating and drinking. So, when you fulfill your job, you should hurry up to your family."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 3001)"
"2709","Sayyiduna Musa (may Allah be pleased with him), and stated that Sayyiduna Suhaib (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated this hadith to him: Whenever the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) intended to enter a town, as soon as he saw the town, he would recite: “O Allah! Lord of the seven heavens and all that they overshadow! Lord of the seven earths and all that they contain beneath them! Lord of the winds and all that they scatter! Lord of the devils and all whom they mislead! We ask You for the goodness of this town, the goodness of its people, and the goodness that is in it, and we seek refuge in You from its evil, the evil of its people, and the evil that is in it.”"
"2710","When the Prophet would return from a trip and see the walls of Al-Madinah, he would speed up his riding camel, and if he was upon a beast, he would agitate it, out of his love for Al-Madinah. (Using translation from Tirmidhī 3441)"
"2711","That whenever the Prophet ﷺ would return from a trip, he would say: “(We are) Returning, repenting, worshipping, and to our Lord directing the praise (Ā’ibūna tā’būna ʿābidūna lirabbinā ḥāmidūn).” (Using translation from Tirmidhī 3440)"
"2712","Sayyiduna Bara’ (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Whenever the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) returned from a journey, he would recite: “We are returning, repenting, and praising our Lord.”"""
"2713","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): \""When a person enters his city at night, he should not go to his wife at night.\"""""
"2714","narrates: We went with the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) to participate in a battle. When we returned, the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: ""You people wait so that the woman with disheveled hair may comb her hair, and the woman (whose husband had been away from home for a long time) may adorn herself."
"2715","The narrator states: When he came to Madinah Munawwarah, the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) instructed him to come to the mosque and perform two rak‘ahs."
"2716","I seek Your protection from the hardship of travel, from facing any distress upon return. O Allah! Fold the earth for us and make our journey easy for us.” When he intended to return, he would recite: “We are returning, repenting, worshipping, and prostrating before our Lord.” When he entered his home, he would recite: “Repenting, repenting, turning towards our Lord (we return home), may He not leave any of our sins remaining.”"",""And when he intended to return"",""he would say"","" 'Returning"","" repenting"","" worshiping"","" and prostrating to our Lord.'"",""And when he entered his house"",""he would say"","" 'Returning"","" repenting to our Lord"","" and pardoning that which does not harm us.'"""""""
"2717","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Why did you not marry a young girl so that you could play with her and she could play with you? I replied: I have sisters, and I preferred to marry a woman who would look after them, comb their hair, and take care of them. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Now you are returning, so when you go home, act wisely. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) By the word ""wisely"" is meant to have intercourse."
"2718","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""No woman should travel for more than three days without a mahram."
"2719","“No woman should travel the distance of three days or more, unless she is with her father, brother, son, husband or a Mahram.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2898)"
"2720","narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""It is not permissible for any woman to undertake a journey of three days except that there is with her a mahram who is permanently unlawful for her (to marry)."
"2721","It is not lawful for a woman to undertake three (days, ) journey except when there is a Mahram with her. (Using translation from Muslim 1339d)"
"2722","It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and the Hereafter to travel for more than three nights journey except when there is a Mahram with her. (Using translation from Muslim 1338c)"
"2723","narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""No woman should travel for two days and two nights except when her husband or a mahram is with her (then it is permissible)."
